CREATED:20250815T143512Z
DESCRIPTION:The J. Samuel Hammond Carillon Recitals are performed on the C
 hapel's 50-bell carillon\, and may be enjoyed al fresco from the beauty o
 f Abele Quad. This recital will be presented rain or shine. \n\nParking i
 s available on a first-come-first-served basis in the Bryan Center garage
  at 125 Science Drive. ADA parking is available in the Bryan Center Surfa
 ce Lot at the same address.\n\nDuke Chapel's fifty-bell carillon is among
  the oldest and largest such instruments in the American South. Both the 
 instrument and the recital series are named in honor of the late J. Samue
 l Hammond (1947-2021)\, University Carillonneur Emeritus\, who played Duk
 e's carillon from 1964 until his retirement in 2018.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20250815T143512Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260419T170000
LAST-MODIFIED:20250815T143512Z
